 | `TF_MINIMAX_WORLD` | MiniMax-M3.1-Flash on CUDA: a whole rank count, 2 at CUDA, set with `TF_MINIMAX_RANK`; unset with it gives one rank |
 | `TF_INKLING2_RANK` | Inkling 2 on CUDA: a whole rank index, 0 or 1 at two ranks, set with `TF_INKLING2_WORLD`; unset with it gives one rank |
 | `TF_INKLING2_WORLD` | Inkling 2 on CUDA: a whole rank count, 2 on CUDA, set with `TF_INKLING2_RANK`; unset with it gives one rank |
+| `TF_INKLING2_KV` | Inkling 2 on CUDA: `fp8` stores the global layers' keys and values as e4m3 with an fp32 scale a token and key head (about half the bytes of a stream); `bf16` (default) keeps them in bf16. Sliding layers stay bf16 |
+| `TF_INKLING2_DRAFT_WEIGHTS` | Inkling 2 on CUDA: `nvfp4` quantises the bundled drafter's projections to NVFP4 at load (round to nearest); `bf16` (default) keeps them as released. Changes acceptance, never output |
+| `TF_INKLING2_PROFILE` | Inkling 2 on CUDA: `1` times a round's phases on each rank and logs a line every 200 rounds (syncs the forward; off by default) |
 | `TF_PROMPT_ROWS` | Native serving: a multiple of 16 from 128 through 2048; unset keeps the chip/family default |
 | `TF_ANE_COLUMNS` | Whole u32 count; zero disables the experimental share; default zero |
 | `TF_METAL4` | Metal: exactly `0` or `1`; `1` sends a family's GPU work through Metal 4 (macOS 26 and later) where the family supports it: the same kernels in the same order, with Metal 4's command queue, allocators, argument tables and barriers, and bit-identical outputs; `0` keeps Metal 3. DeepSeek-V4.1 defaults to `1` where the Mac has Metal 4 (its device test rigs to `0`); Macs without it stay on Metal 3 |
